1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
EMOI, Safe Agent. Give AI a wallet, without giving it the keys to everything. Agent ID: agent.emoi.testnet. Policy: max 1 NEAR per transaction, daily 2 NEAR. Whitelist: emoi01, emoi02.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Success. The agent pays 0.5 NEAR to emoi01, an API and compute provider, within max 1 and daily 2. Transaction: AzefmP7m4VCyi7TUVinQQpZ7ZYsyv6j9H21419uceU67.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Rejected. Send 100 NEAR to attacker.near. Blocked: RecipientNotWhitelisted. Blocked before signing. No transaction hash. No NEAR left the vault.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Rejected. Send 1.5 NEAR to emoi01, whitelisted but over max 1. Blocked: ExceedsMaxPerTx. Blocked before signing. No transaction hash.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Paused. The owner pauses the agent. A transfer attempt is rejected: AgentPaused. Blocked before signing. No transaction hash.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Resumed. The owner resumes the agent. Agent status: Active again. Revoke is terminal: a revoked agent ID can never be re-registered.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
What this proves: the agent spends on its own, within policy. It cannot escape its policy. The owner can pause or revoke at any time. The agent service holds only a Function Call Key: one method, one contract. It never holds the owner's full key.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
EMOI on NEAR testnet. PolicyVault: policy.emoi.testnet. Agent: agent.emoi.testnet. Run locally: scripts/run-local.sh.
